From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:27:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tcpm: Restart discovery after a response timeout

When the partner's response to Discover Identity, Discover SVIDs or
Discover Modes on SOP arrives after tVDMSenderResponse, the VDM state
machine times out, finishes the AMS and never asks again. Discovery
stops at that step, and the partner's alternate modes stay unregistered
until the next attach. On a DisplayPort alternate mode connection that
is a connection without a picture.

Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S with a USB-C DisplayPort adapter: it
answers each discovery request within about 17 ms, but in some cold
boots one answer, to Discover Identity or to Discover Modes, came only
after about 50 ms, after the 30 ms response timeout, and the boot
ended without DisplayPort.

A timeout is not a refusal. Restart discovery from Discover Identity
when one of the three requests times out on SOP, at most three times
per attach; the count is reset on attach and on hard reset.
svdm_consume_identity() clears the modes gathered by the interrupted
pass. Discovery on SOP' keeps its existing handling. A late Discover
Identity or Discover SVIDs response is dropped; a late Discover Modes
response that arrives while the restarted discovery is in flight is
still handled as a mode response.

Not covered: a data role swap restarts discovery without resetting the
count.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: not tested; the restart was not triggered in
the runs.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
index 06692feb6d46..999e999d039e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
@@ -296,6 +296,7 @@ enum frs_typec_current {
 
 #define GET_SINK_CAP_RETRY_MS	100
 #define SEND_DISCOVERY_VDM_RETRY_MS	100
+#define VDM_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT_RETRIES	3
 
 struct pd_mode_data {
 	int svid_index;		/* current SVID index		*/
@@ -607,6 +608,8 @@ struct tcpm_port {
 
 	/* VDM Discovery State to determine message sent */
 	enum vdm_discovery_states vdm_discovery_state;
+	/* Discovery restarts after a response timeout since the last attach */
+	u32 vdm_discovery_timeouts;
 
 	/* PD state for Vendor Defined Messages */
 	enum vdm_states vdm_state;
@@ -2942,6 +2945,34 @@ static unsigned int vdm_ready_timeout(u32 vdm_hdr)
 	return timeout;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A partner that answers Discover Identity, Discover SVIDs or Discover Modes
+ * on SOP only after tVDMSenderResponse has expired is not asked again, so its
+ * alternate modes are never registered. Restart discovery from Discover
+ * Identity, a bounded number of times per attach. svdm_consume_identity()
+ * clears the modes of the interrupted pass. A late Identity or SVIDs response
+ * is dropped; a late Modes response can still be handled.
+ */
+static void tcpm_vdm_discovery_timeout(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	if (port->tx_sop_type != TCPC_TX_SOP)
+		return;
+
+	if (port->ams != DISCOVER_IDENTITY && port->ams != DISCOVER_SVIDS &&
+	    port->ams != DISCOVER_MODES)
+		return;
+
+	if (port->vdm_discovery_timeouts >= VDM_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT_RETRIES)
+		return;
+
+	port->vdm_discovery_timeouts++;
+	tcpm_log(port, "%s timed out, restarting discovery (%u of %u)",
+		 tcpm_ams_str[port->ams], port->vdm_discovery_timeouts,
+		 VDM_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT_RETRIES);
+	tcpm_update_vdm_discovery_state(port, VDM_DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN);
+	mod_vdm_discovery_delayed_work(port, SEND_DISCOVERY_VDM_RETRY_MS);
+}
+
 static void vdm_run_state_machine(struct tcpm_port *port)
 {
 	struct pd_message msg;
@@ -3021,6 +3052,7 @@ static void vdm_run_state_machine(struct tcpm_port *port)
 		break;
 	case VDM_STATE_BUSY:
 		port->vdm_state = VDM_STATE_ERR_TMOUT;
+		tcpm_vdm_discovery_timeout(port);
 		if (port->ams != NONE_AMS)
 			tcpm_ams_finish(port);
 		break;
@@ -5072,6 +5104,7 @@ static int tcpm_src_attach(struct tcpm_port *port)
 	port->partner = NULL;
 
 	port->attached = true;
+	port->vdm_discovery_timeouts = 0;
 	tcpm_update_vdm_discovery_state(port, VDM_DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -5234,6 +5267,7 @@ static int tcpm_snk_attach(struct tcpm_port *port)
 	port->partner = NULL;
 
 	port->attached = true;
+	port->vdm_discovery_timeouts = 0;
 	tcpm_update_vdm_discovery_state(port, VDM_DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -6078,6 +6112,7 @@ static void run_state_machine(struct tcpm_port *port)
 		port->tcpc->set_pd_rx(port->tcpc, false);
 		tcpm_unregister_altmodes(port);
 		port->nr_sink_caps = 0;
+		port->vdm_discovery_timeouts = 0;
 		tcpm_update_vdm_discovery_state(port, VDM_DISCOVERY_UNKNOWN);
 		mod_vdm_discovery_cancel_delayed_work(port);
 		if (port->pwr_role == TYPEC_SOURCE)
